# License

This repository is dual-licensed. A single license could not express the boundary
cleanly, so the boundary is stated here explicitly rather than applying one license
to material it does not fit.

## Dual-licensing boundary

**Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)** applies to the
specification text, documentation and conformance fixture data:

```text
README.md
STATUS.md
CHANGELOG.md
CITATION.cff
LICENSE
spec/**
conformance/negative-fixtures.json
conformance/positive-fixtures.json
conformance/fixture.schema.json
conformance/negative-fixture.schema.json
research/**
```

**Apache License 2.0** applies to the executable code:

```text
conformance/validate.py
tests/**
.github/workflows/**
source-capsule/**
```

`source-capsule/**` is an explicit exception to the CC BY 4.0 documentation and
fixture default above. Its documentation, schemas, fixtures and generated reports
retain the Apache-2.0 license of the migrated source project. See
`source-capsule/LICENSE_SCOPE.md`.

The full Apache-2.0 text is in [`LICENSE-CODE`](LICENSE-CODE). SPDX expression for
the repository as a whole: `CC-BY-4.0 AND Apache-2.0`.

